/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 96 0 R
/E (Problem Definition: Food delivery ecosystems operate in high-velocity environments where supply and demand fluctuate rapidly. Traditional batch data processing models fail to capture intraday meal rushes and dispatch delays in time for operational intervention. Conversely, naive streaming systems that write directly to relational databases suffer from lock contention, high latency, and lack historical auditability.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
117 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 96 0 R
/E (The Proposed Solution: An end-to-end data platform integrating an event-driven streaming ingestion bus \(Apache Kafka\) with an object-storage data lake \(MinIO\) organized in a Medallion architecture. Continuous transformation and cleansing are managed via Apache Spark, while analytical serving is fulfilled by a PostgreSQL Star Schema warehouse, scheduled via Apache Airflow, and visualized via Metabase.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
